From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "AnyBook (ANAL-297)" <noreply@anybook.invalid>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/7] x86_64: leave out NUMA onlining of coherent GPU memory

os_numa_add_gpu_memory() and os_numa_remove_gpu_memory() hot-add GPU memory
to the kernel as a NUMA node on systems where the GPU's memory is
cache-coherent with the CPU (NVLink-C2C on Grace). No x86_64 PCIe system has
that, and the code made the module import add_memory_driver_managed(),
offline_and_remove_memory() and the memory notifier. Report it unsupported
on x86_64, as on kernels without memory hotplug.
---
 kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c b/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
index 9fa7a1a..0e7a238 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia/os-interface.c
@@ -54,6 +54,16 @@
 #include <linux/vmalloc.h>
 #include <linux/pci_regs.h>
 
+/*
+ * Onlining GPU memory as a NUMA node (os_numa_add_gpu_memory) is for coherent
+ * GPU memory, which x86_64 PCIe GPUs do not have (Grace and other C2C hosts
+ * are Arm64). Leave memory hotplug out there.
+ */
+#if defined(NVCPU_X86_64)
+#undef NV_ADD_MEMORY_DRIVER_MANAGED_PRESENT
+#undef NV_OFFLINE_AND_REMOVE_MEMORY_PRESENT
+#endif
+
 extern char *NVreg_TemporaryFilePath;
 
 #define MAX_ERROR_STRING 528
